Sofa for Windows (deploy/windows) carries two programs that aren't Sofa's, each under its own licence, in its own
folder of the installed Sofa:

  vendor/python                       Python 3.14, the Python Software Foundation's embeddable build,
                                      PSF License (vendor/python/LICENSE.txt)
  vendor/ffmpeg                       ffmpeg 9.0.2, Gyan Doshi's Windows build, GNU GPL version 3
                                      (vendor/ffmpeg/LICENSE.txt; where its source is: SOURCE.txt)

Sofa runs ffmpeg as a separate program. tools/windows-deps.py names the exact downloads and their SHA-256.

A Sofa Box card is built from Raspberry Pi OS and other free software (Chromium, mpv, FFmpeg, Luanti and
more), each under its own licence. Every part on a card, with its licence and source, is listed in
deploy/sofa-box/home/credits.json and shown on the box under Settings -> This box -> About -> Credits
and licences. Games whose data is not free software are never on a card; a box installs them only when
its owner asks.

